-> Reference: domains — `Z` (integers), `N` (naturals, ≥ 0), `R` (reals),
-> a Set as a domain (`∈ {..}`/`∈ <set variable>`), and a builtin type
-> name (`∈ String`).
whole ∈ Z
whole > -5
whole < 5
loop whole get integers { yield whole }
assert integers = [-4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]

nat ∈ N
nat < 3
loop nat get naturals { yield nat }
assert naturals = [0, 1, 2]

real ∈ R
real > 0
real < 1
assert real > 0

candidates = {1, 2, 3}
pick ∈ candidates
pick = 2
assert pick ∈ candidates

s ∈ String
s = "hello"
assert s = "hello"
